type: software

title: "SE Pilot: Structural Assurability"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-29"

authors:
  - family-names: Case
    given-names: Denise M.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6165-7389"
    affiliation: "Northwest Missouri State University, School of Computer Science and Information Systems, Maryville, MO, USA"

repository-code: "https://github.com/structural-explainability/se-pilot-structural-assurability"
url: "https://github.com/structural-explainability/se-pilot-structural-assurability"
license: MIT

abstract: >
  Applied research investigating the applicability and limitations
  of claim-relative Structural Assurability when examining concrete
  assurance claims and external evaluation frameworks. The pilot
  develops source-grounded mappings, explicit research questions,
  and reproducible experiments where appropriate. Initial
  investigations examine NIST's TEVV-Athlon framework and the
  UK AI Security Institute's cyber-inability safety-case research,
  with particular attention to available observations, evidentiary
  capabilities, evaluator conditions, trust assumptions, and the
  limits of claim resolution.

keywords:
